      "solution": "$y = \\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{2x + 5} = \\frac{x^{\\frac{1}{2}}}{2x + 5}$\n$\\therefore \\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{2}x^{-\\frac{1}{2}}(2x + 5) - (2) \\times x^{\\frac{1}{2}}}{(2x + 5)^2} \\quad \\{\\text{quotient rule}\\}\n= \\frac{2x + 5 - 4x}{2\\sqrt{x}(2x + 5)^2}\n= \\frac{5 - 2x}{2\\sqrt{x}(2x + 5)^2}$\n\nWhen $x = 4$,\n$\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{5 - 2(4)}{2\\sqrt{4}(2(4) + 5)^2} = \\frac{-3}{2 \\times 2 \\times 169} = -\\frac{3}{676}$.\nSo, the tangent has gradient $-\\frac{3}{676}$.",
